---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { author } from '../data/author';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & disclosure"
  description={`About ${SITE_NAME}: who writes these guides, what we are not, and how we handle sources, money, and corrections.`}
>
  <section class="container prose">
    <h1>About & disclosure</h1>

    <p><strong>{author.name}</strong> — {author.role}.</p>
    <p>{author.bio}</p>

    <div class="callout red">
      <div class="title">What we are not</div>
      <p>{author.disclaimer}</p>
    </div>

    <h2>How we handle money</h2>
    <p>
      This site may earn revenue from digital products and, later, affiliate
      links or advertising. Commercial relationships never change a verdict:
      a quote is measured against published cost data and consumer-rights rules,
      not against who pays us. Any affiliate link is labeled where it appears.
    </p>

    <h2>How we handle numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every cost range carries a source and a month/year ("as of …").</li>
      <li>We never invent a statistic, price, review, or metric.</li>
      <li>When data is an estimate rather than a measured fact, it is labeled.</li>
      <li>Law differs by state; each rights guide names its state and its source.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Pricing and rules change. When a published figure is wrong or out of date,
      we update the page and bump its "Updated" date. The refresh is documented
      in the page itself — not silently edited.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or corrections: <a href="mailto:hello@quoteforensics.com">hello@quoteforensics.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
